<title>CYPRUS: Cyprus accepts Tradigrain tender for barley.</title>
<headline>Cyprus accepts Tradigrain tender for barley.</headline>
<dateline>NICOSIA 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Cyprus Grain Commission said on Friday it accepted a tender from Tradigrain SA Geneve for the supply of 25,000 tonnes of barley for $150.82 per tonne.</p>
<p>Shipment is scheduled before May 20, 1997. The price includes cost and freight, a statement from the grain commission said.</p>
</text>
